  "gaps": [
    "Catalog year/term is not stated on the page.",
    "The credit system is not stated explicitly; 'semester' is inferred from the BA 439 note about the student's 'final semester'.",
    "Specific general education courses for the 37 Integrative General Education credits are not listed in the capture.",
    "The Kirkpatrick Signature Series is required, but its courses and credits are not listed. The capture also does not say whether it counts within the 37 general education credits.",
    "Residency: a minimum of 21 upper-level credit hours (AC or BA courses 300-level or above) in the major must be taken in-residence. Upper-level Common Business Core credits may count toward this. The capture does not tie this rule to specific courses, so no course is flagged institutionalOnly.",
    "Major requirements are stated as 60-63 credit hours depending on Emphasis. The Business Analytics Emphasis requires only two courses (BAN 304, BAN 400; 6 credits), making the major 60 credits. The capture does not state how the remaining 3 credits are allocated (for example, to electives) in that case.",
    "Some emphasis options are listed with variable credits: AC 311 (1 - 3 credits) and the internships BA 487, BA 488 and BA 493 (1 - 3 credits). The capture does not say how a shortfall below 9 emphasis credits is handled.",
    "The Financial Counseling Emphasis includes BA 110 (a 100-level course), while the alternative path requires 300-level or above coursework. Any effect on upper-level or residency totals is not stated.",
    "GPA requirements are policies, not ledger items: overall GPA 2.0, and 2.5 in major AC, BA and ECN courses.",
    "Prerequisites outside the ledger are referenced but not listed as requirements: MA 101 or ALEKS placement, EN 101, EN 102, CA 105, and BSCL 325 and BSCL 415 for BSCL 430. Whether these count toward general education or electives is not stated.",
    "The capture does not state whether core courses such as MA 102, MA 215, ECN 201 and ECN 202 may double-count toward general education.",
    "The page notes that current students should consult BRUIN 'Academic Progress' and that admissions counselors verify minimum graduation requirements. The authoritative academic catalog entry is not captured."
  ],
